<title>UK: Mexico cuts Feb crude price to Europe, Asia/US flat.</title>
<headline>Mexico cuts Feb crude price to Europe, Asia/US flat.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-01-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mexico cut February prices for its Maya and Isthmus crudes to European lifters by 10 cents a barrel but left both grades unchanged for customers in the United States and Asia, an official at state-owned oil company PEMEX said on Monday.</p>
<p>The only increase was for Olmeca crude to U.S. lifters, which will rise 10 cents a barrel to 55 cents above the PEMEX formula, he added.</p>
<p>European lifters will pay formula less $1.85 a barrel for Maya and less 16 cents for Isthmus in February compared with January prices of -$1.75 and -$0.06 respectively.</p>
<p>U.S. customers will continue to pay formula less $1.75 a barrel for Maya and less $1.00 a barrel for Isthmus.</p>
<p>In Asia, Maya will cost formula less $3.20 a barrel and Isthmus formula plus 75 cents, unchanged from January, PEMEX said.</p>
<p>--Mark Thompson, London Newsroom +44 171 542 7930</p>
</text>
